extends ../layout

block content
  section#heartwheels.section
    .container
      h2 Heartwheels

      .gallery-grid.gallery-grid--3col
        img(src="/img/heartwheels/7932613618454906383.jpeg" alt="Heartwheels donation" loading="lazy")
        img(src="/img/heartwheels/IMG_0010.jpeg" alt="Heartwheels donation" loading="lazy")
        img(src="/img/heartwheels/IMG_0011.jpeg" alt="Heartwheels donation" loading="lazy")
        img(src="/img/heartwheels/IMG_9719.jpeg" alt="Heartwheels donation" loading="lazy")
        img(src="/img/heartwheels/IMG_9720.jpeg" alt="Heartwheels donation" loading="lazy")
        img(src="/img/heartwheels/IMG_9726.jpeg" alt="Heartwheels donation" loading="lazy")

      p.
        Taku Hanson was born and raised in Seattle, served his tour in the U.S. Army, and
        settled in Kalispell to be near his sister's family. He, his wife Brenda, and their
        son Tomas were founding members of this chapter, back when we were the Montana Sea
        Hawkers. Like every Sea Hawker, they earned their names: Heartwheel Hawk, Brenda Hawk,
        and Tomas Hawk.

      p.
        In May 2023 the family came home from the Sea Hawkers banquet where Brenda had just
        been named Sea Hawker of the Year by the international booster club. Taku hadn't felt
        right during the trip, so he went in for testing. The diagnosis was stage 4 colon
        cancer that had already spread to other organs. He decided to fight it.

      p.
        Heartwheels started in an infusion chair. The clinic put Taku in a children's treatment
        room for his chemo, and sitting there got him thinking about the kids who usually filled
        it. The next treatment day he brought a Hot Wheels car and asked the nurse to pass it
        along to whichever child was in. A little while later a frail boy walked in, still hooked
        to his IV, to say thank you. He told Taku the car made the hours easier, because now he
        had something new to play with.

      p.
        Taku went home and told Brenda and Tomas about the boy. They cried, then talked for
        hours, and landed on the name Heartwheels. The goal was simple: a small metal car for
        every child going through cancer treatment. Brenda started a Heartwheels Facebook page.
        They collected cars around Kalispell, bought more with their own money, then asked Sea
        Hawkers everywhere for help. Chapters around the world started shipping boxes. By the
        end of 2025, more than 5,000 cars had gone to kids at Logan Health Children's.

      p.
        The staff there told the family what it was doing. Parents and kids were sitting
        together playing with the cars in the children's cancer center. Kids started arriving
        looking forward to picking out a car instead of thinking about why they were there.
        Adult patients began bringing cars of their own to hand to the kids getting chemo
        beside them.

      p.
        Taku gave his time in plenty of other places too. He visited veterans in the hospital
        who had no one else coming to see them, and he and his family supported Mikayla's
        Miracles and Blessings, Special Olympics, and Down syndrome buddies. He kept it up
        while he was in treatment himself, the way Paul Allen asked all of us to leave the
        world better than we found it.

      p.
        At the start of 2026 the doctors told Taku the cancer was moving faster. What he wanted
        was for Heartwheels to keep going without him: one car, one smile, for every kid before
        treatment. He passed away on April 10, 2026 with Brenda and Tomas beside him, just after
        learning he had been named Sea Hawker of the Month.

      p.
        Brenda Hawk and Tomas Hawk are carrying Heartwheels forward, and they want it to grow.
        Rest easy, Taku. You made the world a better place.

  section.section.alt-bg
    .container
      h3 Keep Heartwheels Going

      p.
        Brenda and Tomas are asking Sea Hawkers and 12s everywhere to keep the cars coming.
        Bring new toys to a watch party or mail them to Brenda.

      .cards.cards-three
        .card
          .card-body
            h3 Bring to a Watch Party
            p.
              Drop off new, unopened Hot Wheels — or other small toys — at any of our game day
              watch parties. YSH will handle shipping them to Brenda for you.
            a.btn-outline(href="/#contact") Find a Watch Party
        .card
          .card-body
            h3 Send Cars
            p Mail new, unopened Hot Wheels cars directly to Brenda. Every car makes a difference.
            button.btn-outline(type="button" data-modal="address-modal") Mailing Address
        .card
          .card-body
            h3 Spread the Word
            p.
              Share Heartwheels with friends, family, and your community. The more people
              who know, the more cars we can deliver.
            button.btn-outline#hw-share-btn(type="button" hidden) Share
        .card
          .card-body
            h3 Questions?
            p.
              Reach out through our contact form if you'd like to get involved in another way.
            a.btn-outline(href="/#contact") Get in Touch

  section.section
    .container
      a.btn-outline(href="/#charitable") &larr; Back to Charitable Work

  #address-modal.hw-modal(role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="address-modal-title")
    .hw-modal-backdrop
    .hw-modal-dialog
      button.hw-modal-close(type="button" aria-label="Close") &times;
      h3#address-modal-title Mailing Address
      address.
        Brenda Rosler-Hanson
        #[br] 278 2nd Ave W N
        #[br] Kalispell, MT 59901

  script(src="/js/heartwheels.js")
